config VIDEO_V4L2LOOPBACK
	tristate "V4L2 loopback devices"
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	help
	  Create virtual V4L2 video devices. A process writes frames to the
	  output side of a device and ordinary V4L2 clients capture them.

	  The Surface Pro X uses this for /dev/video63, which spx-ir-bridge
	  feeds from the OV7251 IR camera for face authentication (Howdy).

	  This is upstream v4l2loopback 0.15.4, commit
	  442d720262e150084e7923068fb3c01acc42a253 of
	  https://github.com/umlaeute/v4l2loopback, imported unchanged.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called v4l2loopback.
